@prefix delphi: <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/> .

sub:Head {
  this: a np:Nanopublication ;
    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/flight-climb-glide-law> a delphi:Concept, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Climb from excess power and the range of a steady glide (Lean 4, kernel-checked)" ;
    dct:description "Under a power balance with non-negative losses the climb rate is at most (P_avail − P_req)/W, and a steady unpowered glide from height h with lift equal to weight covers at most h (L/D)max, or h (L/D)max/(1 − δ) when drag is reduced by a fraction δ near the surface." ;
    dct:source "Proved in this project (lean/Delphi/Flight.lean) for the flying-fish audit and the physics thread's coupled simulator (hub items 3 and 4, 2026-10-31); hypotheses named, no paper states it in this form." ;
    skos:notation "c ≤ (P_avail − P_req)/W ; x ≤ h (L/D)max/(1−δ)" ;
    skos:definition """/-- **Steady-glide range.** With no thrust, lift equal to weight, `L/D ≤ (L/D)_max` and the potential energy `W h` spent on drag work `D x` plus non-negative losses, the horizontal distance is at most `h (L/D)_max`. -/
theorem glide_range_le {W h D x LDmax loss Lift : ℝ} (_hW : 0 < W) (hD : 0 < D) (hh : 0 ≤ h)
    (hlift : Lift = W) (hLD : Lift / D ≤ LDmax) (henergy : W * h = D * x + loss) (hloss : 0 ≤ loss) :
    x ≤ h * LDmax"""^^delphi:lean4 ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    delphi:leanDeclaration "Delphi.climbRate" ;
    delphi:leanTheorem "Delphi.glide_range_le", "Delphi.glide_range_le_groundEffect", "Delphi.climbRate_le", "Delphi.climb_nonneg_iff" ;
    delphi:leanVerified "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    skos:scopeNote "Energy and power balances with non-negative losses are the named hypotheses; taxiing thrust, multiple touch-and-go, wind and updrafts are outside the glide model, which is why field glide distances can exceed the bound." ;
    rdfs:comment "Status: kernel-checked (Lean 4 accepted the module with zero sorry and standard axioms only). Not expert-validated. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it; strict neutrality, constant population size, Wright-Fisher reproduction and independent mutant fates (Kimura), fixed fitnesses and haploid inheritance (Fisher), equal fecundity and a 1:1 sex ratio (Maynard Smith) are assumptions written in the module header, not conclusions. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the paper is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/Delphi/Flight.lean>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/flight-climb-glide-law> dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/flight-climb-glide-law> ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-flight-climb-glide-law> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-flight-climb-glide-law> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Lean 4 kernel accepted Delphi.glide_range_le with zero sorry and standard axioms, and rejected 2 deliberately broken variant(s)" ;
    dct:description "Build receipt. Lean (version 4.35.0, x86_64-w64-windows-gnu, commit eb6cafb7290e8bd5f2937522d8d804f58f02bafc, Release); toolchain leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0; Mathlib v4.35.0 (56a005855ea17e0b0958f73ec801ae140b0a1679). lake build exit 0 in 23.2 s with 0 errors; 0 sorry in lean/Delphi/Flight.lean (206 lines). #print axioms for Delphi.glide_range_le, Delphi.glide_range_le_groundEffect, Delphi.climbRate_le, Delphi.climb_nonneg_iff: Classical.choice, Quot.sound, propext only (Lean's standard axioms; no sorryAx). Mutation evidence (lean/mutate.mjs, 2026-10-31T21:58:20.213Z): 2 deliberate change(s) to the statement or the model were each rejected by the compiler: [climb-bound-reversed] Mutant: the climb bound reversed (the excess power over weight claimed to be at most the climb rate); false with positive losses, so the proof must fail. Rejected with 1 error(s): Flight.lean:101:6: error: Tactic `rewrite` failed: Did not find an occurrence of the pattern [glide-range-halved] Mutant: the glide range claimed to be at most half of h (L/D)max; the energy balance allows the full bound, so the proof must fail. Rejected with 2 error(s): Flight.lean:117:25: error: unsolved goals Controls: 16 of 16 unmodified modules accepted by the same command." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/flight-climb-glide-law> ;
    rdfs:comment "This evidence item establishes that the stated theorem follows from the stated model. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it; strict neutrality, constant population size, Wright-Fisher reproduction and independent mutant fates (Kimura), fixed fitnesses and haploid inheritance (Fisher), equal fecundity and a 1:1 sex ratio (Maynard Smith) are assumptions written in the module header, not conclusions. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the paper is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/mutations.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/Delphi/Audit.lean> .
}

